            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Spanish for to speed up, then the Spanish for to circulate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: el motor",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "el motor — \"the engine, the motor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "El motor hace un ruido raro. The engine is making a strange noise."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Arrancar el motor — to start the engine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "motor is a learned borrowing from Latin mōtor \"a mover, one that sets a thing moving\" (Lewis & Short; EtymDB), from movēre \"to move\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
